---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../styles/about-page.css';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="About | Lotus Technologies"
	description="Meet Lotus Technologies — a customer-centric technology partner built around trusted experts, collaborative delivery, and practical solutions."
>
	<div class="about-page">
		<section class="about-hero">
			<div class="about-hero-inner">
				<div>
					<p class="about-eyebrow">About Lotus</p>
					<h1>Your goals. <span>Our expertise.</span></h1>
					<p class="about-hero-copy">
						Lotus Technologies was formed around a simple idea: clients deserve a technology partner that understands the business problem first, brings the right people to the table, and stays accountable from planning through delivery and beyond.
					</p>
				</div>

				<div class="about-hero-visual" aria-label="Lotus combines business context, engineering, design, and customer success around one shared goal">
					<div class="about-orbit"></div>
					<div class="about-orbit two"></div>
					<div class="about-core"><strong>One shared<br />outcome</strong></div>
					<div class="about-node n1"><strong>Business</strong><span>Goals · workflows · outcomes</span></div>
					<div class="about-node n2"><strong>Engineering</strong><span>Architecture · software · systems</span></div>
					<div class="about-node n3"><strong>Experience</strong><span>UX · design · adoption</span></div>
					<div class="about-node n4"><strong>Partnership</strong><span>Transparency · support · trust</span></div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="about-story">
			<div>
				<p class="about-eyebrow">Our Story</p>
				<h2>Built around people we trust.</h2>
			</div>
			<div class="about-story-copy">
				<p>
					Lotus brought together experienced professionals from different areas of technology with one shared vision: create a lean, customer-centric organization capable of solving complex problems without the layers, agendas, and friction clients often encounter with larger vendors.
				</p>
				<p>
					The foundation was personal as much as technical. The people behind Lotus were not selected from a résumé pile. They were engineers, architects, designers, and technology leaders whose work had already earned trust over years of professional relationships.
				</p>
				<p>
					That model still shapes how we work today. We assemble the expertise a problem actually requires, keep communication direct, and work alongside the client instead of disappearing behind a delivery process.
				</p>
				<div class="about-story-callout">Technology is the tool. Solving the business problem is the goal.</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="about-values-wrap">
			<div class="about-values">
				<div class="about-values-head">
					<p class="about-eyebrow">How We Work</p>
					<h2>The principles are simple.</h2>
				</div>
				<div class="about-values-grid">
					<article class="about-value"><span class="about-value-num">01</span><h3>Transparency</h3><p>Clients should understand what is happening, why decisions are being made, and where the project stands.</p></article>
					<article class="about-value"><span class="about-value-num">02</span><h3>Honesty</h3><p>We recommend what fits the problem—not what happens to be easiest or most profitable for us to sell.</p></article>
					<article class="about-value"><span class="about-value-num">03</span><h3>Precision</h3><p>Good execution begins with understanding the real requirement and carrying that context through implementation.</p></article>
					<article class="about-value"><span class="about-value-num">04</span><h3>Collaboration</h3><p>Your team stays part of the process. Shared decisions produce better solutions and fewer surprises.</p></article>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="about-team">
			<div class="about-team-head">
				<div>
					<p class="about-eyebrow">Our Team</p>
					<h2>Different disciplines. One team.</h2>
				</div>
				<p class="about-team-intro">The original Lotus team brought together specialists across customer success, software architecture, web development, design, security, telecommunications, Microsoft technologies, and user experience.</p>
			</div>

			<div class="about-team-grid">
				<article class="about-person featured">
					<div class="about-portrait portrait-customer" aria-hidden="true"><span class="portrait-head"></span><span class="portrait-body"></span><svg viewBox="0 0 120 120"><path d="M20 84h22l9-10h19l9 10h21"/><circle cx="29" cy="38" r="5"/><circle cx="91" cy="38" r="5"/><path d="M34 38h18M68 38h18M60 52v18"/></svg></div>
					<h3>Richard Sampson</h3><p>CTO · Director of Customer Success</p>
					<details><summary>About Richard →</summary><div>Technology has been a lifelong interest, beginning with programming as a child and later developing into a career spanning customer-facing technology roles, solution delivery, and the formation of Lotus Technologies.</div></details>
				</article>
				<article class="about-person featured">
					<div class="about-portrait portrait-architecture" aria-hidden="true"><span class="portrait-head"></span><span class="portrait-body"></span><svg viewBox="0 0 120 120"><rect x="16" y="24" width="22" height="18" rx="4"/><rect x="82" y="24" width="22" height="18" rx="4"/><rect x="49" y="78" width="22" height="18" rx="4"/><path d="M38 33h15M67 33h15M60 42v36"/></svg></div>
					<h3>Andy Pham</h3><p>Director · Software Architecture</p>
					<details><summary>About Andy →</summary><div>UC San Diego computer science graduate with both bachelor's and master's degrees, bringing deep software engineering and enterprise architecture experience to the team.</div></details>
				</article>
				<article class="about-person">
					<div class="about-portrait portrait-web" aria-hidden="true"><span class="portrait-head"></span><span class="portrait-body"></span><svg viewBox="0 0 120 120"><rect x="18" y="24" width="84" height="58" rx="7"/><path d="M18 39h84M28 31h3M37 31h3M46 31h3M32 55l12 10-12 10M57 74h28"/></svg></div>
					<h3>Aaron Mishra</h3><p>Director · Web Development</p><details><summary>About Aaron →</summary><div>Web technology specialist with undergraduate and graduate training in computer science and experience leading development across startup and enterprise environments.</div></details>
				</article>
				<article class="about-person">
					<div class="about-portrait portrait-design" aria-hidden="true"><span class="portrait-head"></span><span class="portrait-body"></span><svg viewBox="0 0 120 120"><circle cx="31" cy="34" r="9"/><rect x="52" y="25" width="45" height="18" rx="5"/><rect x="22" y="67" width="75" height="18" rx="5"/><path d="M31 43v24M43 76h9"/></svg></div>
					<h3>Peter Adhikari</h3><p>Director · UX & Design</p><details><summary>About Peter →</summary><div>Engineer and designer focused on translating product requirements into polished front-end experiences and user-centered interfaces.</div></details>
				</article>
				<article class="about-person">
					<div class="about-portrait portrait-security" aria-hidden="true"><span class="portrait-head"></span><span class="portrait-body"></span><svg viewBox="0 0 120 120"><path d="M60 19l29 11v23c0 21-12 35-29 46-17-11-29-25-29-46V30z"/><rect x="49" y="48" width="22" height="19" rx="4"/><path d="M53 48v-6a7 7 0 0 1 14 0v6"/></svg></div>
					<h3>Tracy Reed</h3><p>Security Architect</p><details><summary>About Tracy →</summary><div>CISSP and RHCE security specialist with deep experience in cloud security, container vulnerability management, intrusion detection, Linux, UNIX, and systems architecture.</div></details>
				</article>
				<article class="about-person">
					<div class="about-portrait portrait-telecom" aria-hidden="true"><span class="portrait-head"></span><span class="portrait-body"></span><svg viewBox="0 0 120 120"><circle cx="60" cy="61" r="5"/><path d="M60 56V31M46 45a20 20 0 0 1 28 0M37 36a33 33 0 0 1 46 0M60 66v20M45 86h30"/></svg></div>
					<h3>Jerry Sokol</h3><p>Telecommunications Architect</p><details><summary>About Jerry →</summary><div>Technology and customer-operations leader experienced in taking software and hardware products from concept through worldwide delivery and translating technology for business stakeholders.</div></details>
				</article>
				<article class="about-person">
					<div class="about-portrait portrait-microsoft" aria-hidden="true"><span class="portrait-head"></span><span class="portrait-body"></span><svg viewBox="0 0 120 120"><rect x="26" y="28" width="28" height="28"/><rect x="66" y="28" width="28" height="28"/><rect x="26" y="68" width="28" height="28"/><rect x="66" y="68" width="28" height="28"/></svg></div>
					<h3>Robert Campbell</h3><p>Microsoft Lead Architect</p><details><summary>About Robert →</summary><div>Long-time Microsoft-stack developer with experience spanning Visual Basic, ASP.NET, MVC, Azure, and enterprise application development.</div></details>
				</article>
				<article class="about-person">
					<div class="about-portrait portrait-ux" aria-hidden="true"><span class="portrait-head"></span><span class="portrait-body"></span><svg viewBox="0 0 120 120"><rect x="22" y="25" width="76" height="62" rx="8"/><circle cx="42" cy="48" r="7"/><path d="M55 43h27M55 52h20M34 70h48M88 94l-8-12"/></svg></div>
					<h3>Vy Nguyen</h3><p>User Experience Lead</p><details><summary>About Vy →</summary><div>Front-end and UX specialist with experience across modern JavaScript stacks, multinational client work, mentoring, and continuous learning.</div></details>
				</article>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="about-close">
			<div>
				<h2>We would rather be your partner than your vendor.</h2>
				<p>Bring us the business problem. We will help determine what the technology needs to do.</p>
			</div>
			<a href="/contact">Discuss Your Challenge</a>
		</section>
	</div>
</BaseLayout>
